Beep: backport service_type = "classic" onto shairport-sync 4.3.2

Lets an AirPlay-2 build advertise ONLY classic AirPlay 1 (RAOP) at runtime,
selected by 'general.service_type = "classic";' in the config file:
  - do not advertise the _airplay._tcp (AirPlay 2) mDNS service (regtype2 stays NULL),
  - skip the nqptp requirement (classic RAOP has no PTP), so it starts without nqptp.
Any other value keeps the default AirPlay 2 behaviour. Mirrors upstream 5.1's option
so a future version bump is a no-op. See docs/CONVERGED-IMAGE-DESIGN.md.

--- a/shairport.c
+++ b/shairport.c
@@ -341,6 +341,12 @@
   }
 #endif
 }
